; DOMAIN: kolyvagin-euler-system [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: For E/Q of conductor N and imaginary quadratic K satisfying the Heegner hypothesis, Kolyvagin uses the norm-compatible system of Heegner points y_c on E over ring class fields K_c (c squarefree product of Kolyvagin primes l inert in K with a_l and l+1 both ker-annihilating mod p). The Kolyvagin derivative operators D_c = prod_l D_l (D_l = sum_{i} i*sigma_l^i built from Gal(K_c/K_1)) applied to y_c yield classes; combined with Chebotarev and the Galois structure, one obtains cohomology classes c(l) in H^1(K, E[p]) whose local restrictions are controlled — trivial away from l, and at l governed by the reduction of y_c. These derived classes annihilate the p-Selmer group: if y_K is non-torsion then Sel_p(E/K) has rank 1 and Sha(E/K)[p^infty] is finite, giving rank(E/K)=1 and finiteness of Sha — the rank<=1 case of BSD (with Gross-Zagier supplying non-torsion <=> L'(E/K,1)!=0). Bridge: genesis_heegner_points (input system y_c and non-torsion y_K criterion) + genesis_selmer_group (target Sel_p(E/K) bounded/annihilated) + genesis_euler_system (Kolyvagin system is the archetypal Euler system, derivative classes + local conditions).
(= (kolyvagin-primes $E $K) (inert-primes-with (annihilate-mod-p (frob-trace $E) (plus l 1))))
(= (derivative-operator $c) (product-over-l (sum-index-sigma (galois (Kc $c) (K1)))))
(= (derived-class $E $K $c) (image (derivative-operator $c) (heegner-point-system $E $K $c)))
(= (annihilates-selmer $E $K) (bounds (derived-class $E $K) (selmer-p $E $K)))
(= (kolyvagin-theorem $E $K) (implies (non-torsion (trace-to-field $E $K)) (and (rank-one (E $K)) (finite (sha-p $E $K)))))